This is my first ascension ever in Slash'Em and the first ascension for a
very very long time (1993/4-ish had a few with vanilla NetHack) so I'm
claiming my First-ish Ascension Post :)

Mick Dundee the archeologist entered the Dungeons of Doom with much caution
given the fact that about 20 of his bretheren had preceeded him quite
recently only to be horribly killed before they had passed the Oracle.  He
crept into the Gnomish Mines and slunk down to mine town.  Mine town was an
unaligned altar but luckily a foolhardy dwarvish thief happened to have a
dwarvish mattock.  Mick quickly discarded the old pick-axe and started
swinging the dwarvish haymaker until he could be so luckily as to find
saber.  After yo-yoing up to the regular dungeon and down to the mall to
pick up a few more supplies (pitiful mall, really), Mick headed down into
the deeper mines.  At this point he had a few dogs and cats with him that
he kept in line with his magic whistle.  On the "bottom" level in the mines
(one above the Gnome King) he found a lamp burning over a bones pile.
Another Mick Dundee body and this one with a bright and shiny dwarvish
mattock (ok, I remembered the previous game that it was a +2 rustproofed
one so made the swap) By now Mick was getting pretty proficient with the
mattock and could do a good whack of damage but was still runnnig around in
a fedora and a leather jacket.  (I was trying to run my arch as a semi-mage
so was looking for not magic blocking armor).  (The dogs and cats didn't
make it past the mines.  He tried having a few horsies later on but they
always find teleport level traps and disappear.)

Mick looked forward to finding pile after pile of old explorer remainents
due to the long list of brothers who preceded him... but that one pile in
the mines was it... (except for a very important one to come!)

Eventually Mick started to collect the good stuff.  He had a bag of holding
from the mines, a "oR from sokoban, and he made it to the quest.  Now, this
was the first time I'd ever had a Archaeologist get to the quest in 
Slash'em,
so I was getting pretty pumped!  But rather than dive in and get that Orb of
Detection, I decided to rein Mick back keep preparing for it for a few more
levels yet.

He found more special levels but also avoided most of them... best save
your strength.  Eventually he used a magic lamp to pray for Grayswandir and
it was delivered!  Finally he could use another weapon other than the 
mattock.

Money was never a problem even early on, due to ensuring at each level that
if there was a vault, he'd find it.  He made a few trips back to Mine Town
and donated heavily to the local clergy to maximize his natural AC.
He got some speed boots in a shop.  Found some gauntlets of power.  


He found a level with a barracks and enchanted a submachinegun to +5 and
took to carrying around 200 bullets with him as he went, picking up more at
the Castle and from the odd wandering soldier or lieutentant.  Wishes were
not an issue.  Mick had 3 magic lamps in the bag and found 2 wands of
wishing (one from the Castle... btw, I didn't think multiple /oW was
possible?) (and later picked up 2 more wands of wishing from a bones 
pile...)
But he was saving them "for later"... later never came actually.

Eventually he had the good fortune to find Ludius and knocked all the
soldiers on the head as they stepped into the portal room, one by one.  
Now he had a huge stockpile of bullets if he cared to come back and dip into
it from time to time.

He headed into Gehenomm but I was worried.  His AC was only -15-ish...
not nearly good enough I thought.  He had polypiled next to an altar on
level 35 and used the enchant armor scrolls to pump up all his stuff but
he only had his gauntlets, speed boots and helmet of brilliance.  
(I was still trying to run him as a semi-mage, and not working badly at
all except for havnig to pull his gloves off all the time - his magic 
missile
was deadly and he found spells useful quite often, but he could never
keep his mana up!)

Somewhere along the line he had found the Sword of Justice and then
later was crowned the hand of elbereth which gave him "basic" in
longsword ability.  From this time until the Wizard run he was dual
wielding Grayswandir and Justice. But for the Wiz run he opted to usually
hae the shield of reflection going so he could wear the "oLS.

And then... it happened... he found "The Icicle".

Lemme digress briefly about "The Icicle"... the Icicle was an ice mage
who thought he could ascend.  He had it all, great armor, great weapons,
great spells, great hitpoints...  Mick found what happened to The Icicle,
why he never became a demigod ... "choked on a lichen"  (yuk yuk).

The Icicle had lots of stuff, including +7 hawaiin shirt, +5 robe of power,
+5 shield of reflection, +4 GDSM, +4 Gauntlets of Defense.  After suiting
up, Mick was at AC -53 and at this point he had around 300 HP.  Not only
that, but Icicle had 5 healthstones, coupled with Mick's 1, that made 6.  
That gives a powerful healing boost... I thought Mick was getting close
to being ready.

Unfortunately, when taking out Frankenstiens Tower I thought "hey, what
does eating a genetic engineer do?"  It polymorphs you into a gray
dragon, ripping your +7 shirt and your +4 cloak in the process, thats
what it does!  ARGH!!!

Anyway, live and learn, he continued down and soon had scoped out the
vibrating square.  Geez, this was easy?  Of course, he was fighting a bone
devil with a wand of digging most of the way.. falling down holes and
such...  didn't I miss some demons?  Well, they were still there on the way
up.  I found that a good submachinegun works wonders on a stair-sitting
demon from 10 paces.  Really, I recommend it!  Virtually all named demons
were machinegunned as a matter of principle.  However, another good lesson
was learned from Asmodeus (I think).  He blinded me.  And surrounded me
with pets.  Thats ok... I don't need to see, I'll cut my way out of here.
Hey, something here that I can't see with telepathy?  No problem... hack
hack hack... hey, why am I turning green?  How do you cure green slime?
Umm... fire?  Break this wand of fireball..  no effect... um.... quick,
"oLS!  Whew!  Died once, lets try not to do that again!

Being extremely concerned that this game was going way too well and there
was much too much chance that YASD was on the way, I (a) did a bunch of
research on newsgroup and (b) had Mick march all the way up and down
the dungeon ensuring that the path was dug and clear all the way.  No
mistakes.  As well, genocided L, ; and h and nurse danced his way up to
HP 380.

Ok, a trip back to Ft. Lud, he picked up 1000 bullets, enchanted to +4 and
stashed them in the BoH in 100 bullet packets.  Mick was burdened, but
I couldn't see lightening all the way to unburdened, so if you are going
to be burdened, might as well pack in some ammo.

Down to the Wizard's Tower.  Mick had ditched the GDSM because I thought I
wanted him to cast more spells.  (Note: this is slashem, DSM blocks magic
by 30%) This came in handy using Jump across the wizard's moat but that was
about it.  The Wiz was a bit of a pain but after Mick discovered
that... "ammo?  use it or lose it" philosphy he was managable.  (I was
really lucky in that he didn't curse much stuff). (I later gave up on
casting spells and regretted ditching the GDSM, especially after the wiz
disintegrated Mick's robe.. and is there any way to prevent that 
disintegration
of armor??)

Down to the square, light the candles, ring the bell, recite the
incantation.  Mick's motto : "don't let a Priest of Moloch next to you if
you can help it.  I've still got bullets and I'm still shooting."  That
submachine gun was getting pretty hot. Ratatatatat. "Got the Amulet, lets
hoof it!"


On the way up, the Wiz disintegrated his robe and his cloak and his
shield...  "bigad, I'm running out of armor!"  Also, ran into an unlucky
streak and went from Exp Lev 26 to 18 in short order (incidentally, I think
this was due to Rodney stealing the Orb of Detection that was giving Mick
level drain resistance, and then a demon happening to have a wand of
draining before Mick could get the Orb back... that was a tad scary).

Luckily, he stopped by at the Icicle's remains on the way up and pilfered a
fresh set of armor - deep dragon scales and a +0 shield of reflection.
He even stopped off at the friendly altar on level 35 and polypiled some
more enchant armor scrolls to get the deep dragon scales setup properly.
(That was scary... right after he put his armor back on, poof - Rodney
shows up.  If he had been just a few minutes earlier, Mick woudl have been
nearly in the buff!  That was dumb!)


Anyway, run run run, pant pant pant, shoot shoot shoot.  Astral plane!
Thanks to my newsgroup helpers, I had 4 scrolls of gold detection that
found the portals for me.  I had a ring of levitation and an amulet of
flying.  My only scare was on the plane of Air... Mick was getting gobbled
by air elemental after air elemental and he was going down in HP.... 200...
150... 100... 50...  16!  Hmmmm.  "I have an "oLS on.  Can I pray on the
Astral plane?  I'll risk it... you BETCHA I can pray!" Mick is back in the
swing.  Mick made it past that one sticky bit and that was the only
dangerous part of the astral planes.

Finally he makes it to the top temple level.  Pestilence?  Death?  I bet
these guys kick butt.  Best follow the previous plan, shoot them before
they get close.  Mick continued putting his submachine gun again to good
use.  He was running out of ammo but as you will see, he made it with 16
slugs left in the magazine.  Tell you the truth, after finding the Icicle
bones pile everything after that was pretty easy...  or do I mean pretty
lucky?

Lots of lessons learned... like don't mess with green slime and don't eat
genetic engineers while wearing your best armor.  Also, use "enlighten" to
find out what you have and what you are missing.  I used it to figure out
that the Orb of Detection gave me MR.  As such, GDSM was overkill.  But I
had found silver dragon scales and discarded them...  If I had been paying
attention I could have used SDSM for reflection and then dual wielded.

I must say... the submachinegun strategy paid off in spades in this
game... and was fun too!  Just imagining stuffing the gun into Rodneys
chest and saying "Dodge this!"

But... what is the point of the eye of the beholder?  
And why did I carry the Keys of Chaos and Neutrality?  I thought I would
need them for the doors on the top temple level but I didnt' seem to.

Whew.


